1
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:03,360
Cinderella

2
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:13,420
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:20,020
Moon Geun Young

4
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:24,180
Cheon Jeong Myeong

5
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:27,270
Seo Woo

6
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:30,520
Taecyeon

7
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:33,250
Lee Mi Sook

8
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,230
Kim Gap Soo

9
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:44,410
Cinderella's Sister

10
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:10,200
Won't you let go?

11
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,010
Come on, Kang Sook.

12
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:15,400
Ms. Kang Sook. Ms. Kang Sook.
Episode 1

13
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:18,080
Won't you let go?

14
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:22,000
Didn't I say I would stay over? Please forgive me just this once.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,130
Remove your hands, you bastard.

16
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:31,600
What can I do huh?

17
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:35,480
I will do all that you say. Just say it.

18
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:43,530
Did you make me like this because you will do what I say?

19
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:48,010
That's not what I did.

20
00:01:48,010 --> 00:01:49,580
Alcohol...

21
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:53,440
I don't want to hear it, you bastard. Move your face!

22
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:57,970
So, didn't I say don't come near me when I drink?

23
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:00,660
What can I do, this body is so pretty.

24
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:03,360
Go away!

25
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:13,600
Did you just throw that? Did you just throw that at me?

26
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:15,600
- Nui ( Sister)
- Shut your mouth!

27
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,880
Because of your blabbering

28
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:19,710
Nui, aren't you going to give me something to eat?

29
00:02:19,710 --> 00:02:21,920
- Why are you eating this up all by yourself?
- Don't you hear that?

30
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:25,150
= Stop!
- Where are you going do you want to die?

31
00:02:25,150 --> 00:02:26,140
Move!

32
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:30,590
I don't know when I'll get to eat food at a table again like this.

33
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:35,130
I have to eat as if it's my last. Don't talk to me.

34
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:38,130
Are you going to leave?

35
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:42,720
It's all your fault, you woman.

36
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:46,540
Nui, if you're going to leave then this is my final meal.

37
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:48,910
There won't be anyone to cook for me once you leave.

38
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:51,720
You want to die?

39
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:53,630
You want to kill me? Go ahead and kill me!

40
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:56,830
I'll kill you. You die, you die...

41
00:02:56,830 --> 00:03:00,720
You made this happen! It's all your fault.

42
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:03,560
You're just asking to die, aren't you?

43
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,790
Kill me! Go ahead and kill me then!

44
00:03:05,790 --> 00:03:09,690
Listen carefully to what I have to say.

45
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:13,110
It doesn't matter where you end up or where you live,

46
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:17,860
I'll find you and take care of you for the rest of your life.

47
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:19,870
Believe what I say.

48
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:22,420
No! Eun Jo!

49
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:30,380
Say you are sorry!

50
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:34,150
What are you doing, you bitch?

51
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:40,150
Have you gone crazy?

52
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:59,350
Song Eun Jo is Han Jeong Woo's girl forever.

53
00:04:06,270 --> 00:04:08,630
Nui, where are you going?

54
00:04:08,630 --> 00:04:10,620
Nui!

55
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,980
Please.

56
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:26,410
- Please, please. Please, wait.
- No!

57
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:30,230
Hey, this is all ripped up. How can I run away looking like this? I must get changed.

58
00:04:30,230 --> 00:04:32,730
Do you think this is the time to worry about that? Hurry up and follow me!

59
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:34,400
Kang Sook!

60
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:36,750
Hurry up, let's go.

61
00:04:38,150 --> 00:04:40,090
Hurry up.

62
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:47,160
Don't go.

63
00:04:51,450 --> 00:04:53,660
Come this way immediately.

64
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:02,540
Let's hurry up.

65
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:15,360
Don't go. Don't go!

66
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:18,080
Don't go.

67
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,210
Kang Sook!

68
00:05:19,210 --> 00:05:22,200
Noona, don't get caught... Goodbye!

69
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,960
Kang Sook, I'm sorry.

70
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,090
Kang Sook.

71
00:05:27,090 --> 00:05:28,990
You can't.

72
00:05:30,310 --> 00:05:33,620
If I catch you two, you're dead.

73
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:38,370
Noona. Eat well and stay healthy!

74
00:05:44,930 --> 00:05:47,660
Ahjussi. Do you want to kill me?

75
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:52,150
If you're going to kill me, will you wait until I finish eating?

76
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:56,400
We don't even have a plan. No plan! Without any money in our pockets, what are we going to do?

77
00:05:56,400 --> 00:06:00,130
Have we ever had any money before? We've never had money every time we ran away...

78
00:06:00,130 --> 00:06:03,390
We have nowhere to go. What's the point of getting on the train? There's nowhere to get off.

79
00:06:03,390 --> 00:06:06,030
Anywhere! As long as it's not here!

80
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:08,900
You make no sense. No sense at all.

81
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:10,780
Ahjussi, take us back where you picked us up.

82
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:12,740
Just go on to the train station, Ahjussi.

83
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:15,680
Ahjussi, if you want to get your fare, go back.

84
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,610
We can't miss the 4.30 train. Hurry up, Ahjussi!

85
00:06:18,610 --> 00:06:21,670
- You brat!
- Do you really want to go back after getting beaten up so much?

86
00:06:21,670 --> 00:06:25,520
You said there was nothing more to take from him!

87
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:28,630
Why are you crawling back to that man whom you can't get anything from to just get beaten until your back is bruised?

88
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:30,910
Why are you screaming at me when you don't know a thing, you little wretch!

89
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:33,270
Don't cuss at me!

90
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:36,920
- Ahjussi!
- Ahjussi!

91
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:40,330
Get out. I can't drive because you're too noisy.

92
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:41,520
Both of you get out.

93
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:45,230
Ahjussi, go back to where we weren before.

94
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:47,230
Really! This crazy woman!

95
00:06:47,230 --> 00:06:50,790
Mom, Is this what you really want?

96
00:07:00,030 --> 00:07:04,930
If this is what you wanted to get from him, I took it so we can just go now.

97
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:13,140
Ahjussi, hurry up and take us to the train station, what are you doing?

98
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:16,950
If we miss our train, are you going to be responsible for it and take us? Hurry up to the train station!

99
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:28,290
Consider this to be your fate in life.

100
00:07:28,290 --> 00:07:31,260
You were about to give it to Ajumma Kang Sook anyway.

101
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:33,660
You thought she would grab it and run away. So that's why you hid it.

102
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,610
Bring Dae Bong to me.

103
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:38,900
Dae... Dae Bong? What do you want with that gangster?

104
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,370
Do you want a beating?

105
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:42,560
No. I don't.

106
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,170
Myeongbong Station

107
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:00,750
Look here. What time does that train arrive at the next station?

108
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:01,900
It arrives at 5.00 PM.

109
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:04,150
- Can we get there by that time?
- We can.

110
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:05,700
Let's go.

111
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:09,460
How could you pack this way?

112
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,970
What's all this?

113
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:13,880
Are we going to a fashion show?

114
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,760
This is the best one you packed but to wear this,

115
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,700
I have to redo my hair and retouch my make up.

116
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:22,410
Is there a beauty salon on this train?

117
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:30,430
Noona, I thought I might get beaten to death, so I went to get Dae Bong.

118
00:08:30,430 --> 00:08:33,040
Don't let him catch you and stay safe.

119
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:36,300
If you ever get caught by him, your bones won't be left.

120
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,990
I won't get caught. Hang up.

121
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:46,710
Who asked you to do this, you bad girl?

122
00:08:46,710 --> 00:08:50,020
Don't you dare to curse. It makes you sound uneducated.

123
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:52,010
You are a thief!

124
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:56,690
When she is in a good mood, she cusses.

125
00:08:56,690 --> 00:08:59,630
If she is in a bad mood also, she cusses.

126
00:08:59,630 --> 00:09:01,400
Thank you.

127
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:08,100
She's a mother but that's how she lives. Please understand.

128
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:12,530
She does far worse things like they are nothing.

129
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:15,350
Do you think you'd like to have a mother like her?

130
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:51,280
Mom! Mom!

131
00:09:58,130 --> 00:10:00,350
- Move. Get out of the way!
- Why?

132
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:03,650
- Get out of the way!
- What's wrong with them?

133
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:32,390
My mom's had more than a million men.

134
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:40,950
Before she could give me father number 1000...

135
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:46,570
I've decided to abandon her.

136
00:11:12,450 --> 00:11:15,560
Mum. Quickly, run.

137
00:11:20,460 --> 00:11:22,160
Over there!

138
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:30,450
But in the end, it became like this.

139
00:11:30,450 --> 00:11:32,390
Darn it...

140
00:11:42,690 --> 00:11:44,050
Hey, get out of the way!

141
00:11:44,050 --> 00:11:46,020
Away.

142
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:48,080
Aigoo, get the heck out the way, wench.

143
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,700
You can just cut ahead!

144
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:52,140
How can I go first with these clothes? I mean it's silk!

145
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:54,360
Is that important right now?

146
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:58,590
Stop, punks.

147
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:00,520
She's over there.

148
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:03,150
Move out of the way.

149
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,200
Ah, what do we do now?

150
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:36,140
Oh, what should we do?

151
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:50,350
Goo Hyo Sun

152
00:12:50,350 --> 00:12:53,790
Ms. Song Kang Sook. Open the door!

153
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:11,550
Daeseong True Wine Makers

154
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:29,200
Stop, stop, stop.

155
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:36,660
Why didn't you pick up your phone? I have to transfer schools right away.

156
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:42,340
I don't know what it's about, but if you're here at this time it means you've skipped class.

157
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:45,940
If I hear the reason and it's nothing big, I'll scold you.

158
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:53,730
That woman said she'd come and find me at my school soon but the ring has disappeared, the ring, I tell you.

159
00:13:53,730 --> 00:13:55,040
Hello, good work.

160
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,820
Oh, you came?

161
00:13:58,270 --> 00:14:03,250
During the Korean class, when I saw the teacher wearing her ring, the memory came back to me.

162
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:06,690
When I was coming back from the class trip, I definitely had it on.

163
00:14:06,690 --> 00:14:09,600
But after that I haven't seen it.

164
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,490
I even went home.

165
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:14,650
I can't find it no matter what.

166
00:14:14,650 --> 00:14:16,660
What do I do?

167
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:19,990
- Hello from Daeseong True Wine Makers.
- Oh, you're here?

168
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:23,910
I'm in really big trouble.

169
00:14:23,910 --> 00:14:29,730
If I say I've lost the ring, the kid certainly looked like someone who'd maul my face.

170
00:14:29,730 --> 00:14:32,100
What am I going to do?

171
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:35,300
My president says he will come by the day after tomorrow.

172
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:37,100
Please give our regards to your president as well.

173
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:38,300
Yes, you've worked hard.

174
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:40,400
Yes, sir. Thank you.

175
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:46,810
In any case, I think I need to transfer schools.

176
00:14:46,810 --> 00:14:48,410
Where should I go?

177
00:14:48,410 --> 00:14:50,860
Should I go far away to some place like Seoul?

178
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:56,390
The MP3 you lost the last time, you found it at the president's library after a week, right?

179
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:58,640
So what?

180
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:01,930
The keepsake T-shirt you bought at H.O.T.'s last concert,

181
00:15:01,930 --> 00:15:05,250
didn't you say you found the housekeeper grandma using it as a rag after half a year?

182
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:06,890
Grandma is really mean.

183
00:15:06,890 --> 00:15:10,850
I mean, how can she use my Oppa Kangta as a rag?

184
00:15:10,850 --> 00:15:16,090
You've also lost the watch the president bought you as a commencement present, right?

185
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:19,290
How did you know?

186
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:21,370
I know since you left it in my room.

187
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:24,780
How much was I looking for that?

188
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:28,420
Is there anything you've lost forever?

189
00:15:32,550 --> 00:15:37,920
I'm asking if within the things you've lost at home, is there something you've never been able to find?

190
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:42,190
There wasn't.

191
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:44,360
Then it's fine.

192
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,650
It hurts.

193
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:56,940
Go in quickly.

194
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:59,850
I am in big trouble wasting time because of you.

195
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:03,500
I have two more places I have to go to.

196
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:05,670
Bro.

197
00:16:07,450 --> 00:16:10,860
You're mine.

198
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,400
What?

199
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:18,150
If you say the moon is rectangular, then I think it is rectangular.

200
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:20,780
If you say salt is sweet and sugar is salty,

201
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:25,200
I am going to gulp down salt water and spew out sugar water.

202
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:30,220
Since you say I can find the ring, it feels like it's never been lost.

203
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:33,090
Did I lose a ring?

204
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:35,530
Why do you talk so much you little thing?

205
00:16:35,530 --> 00:16:37,380
I'm busy.

206
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:40,990
If I get fired because I can't finish my work while helping you, will you take responsibility?

207
00:16:40,990 --> 00:16:47,420
Since you're mine, you can't get married to anyone. Okay?

208
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:51,230
I don't want even Jeon Do Yeon or Go So Young.

209
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:57,300
Oppa, Bye.

210
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:22,820
What is that?

211
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,610
I should have snuck in during the recess.

212
00:17:54,430 --> 00:17:57,490
10th Grade - Homeroom No. 4

213
00:17:58,570 --> 00:18:01,210
Goo Hyo Seon

214
00:18:04,970 --> 00:18:06,790
It must be you.

215
00:18:08,850 --> 00:18:11,560
At my call you

216
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:13,110
Come quickly.

217
00:18:13,110 --> 00:18:16,120
It's so horrible that I could die.

218
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:19,360
How could you leave me here alone and go off by yourself?

219
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:20,990
How could you do that?

220
00:18:20,990 --> 00:18:25,560
If I had left with you, that human would have thought we were running away again and would have followed me.

221
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:28,950
I will find the ring, take care of it and come straight back for you.

222
00:18:28,950 --> 00:18:32,810
Finish it off? What and how are you going to finish it off?

223
00:18:32,810 --> 00:18:34,620
You don't need to know.

224
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:35,550
Mom.

225
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:37,000
Ajumma!

226
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,560
Oh, are you all done?

227
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:41,750
Where is your house?

228
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:47,060
I mean ...

229
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:53,000
What can I do about it?

230
00:18:57,260 --> 00:19:00,040
But, why did you come Ajumma?

231
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,930
I thought that kid Song Eun Jo would come.

232
00:19:02,930 --> 00:19:04,510
She's my daughter.

233
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:06,770
But, do we have to go for a while?

234
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:08,190
We're almost there.

235
00:19:08,190 --> 00:19:10,670
Back then, how did it go with those bad guys?

236
00:19:10,670 --> 00:19:15,500
The men that came to find you in the bathrooms? Did the police lock them up?

237
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:16,920
Did you give them a taste of the prison food?

238
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:19,120
If it's far, let's take a taxi.

239
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:22,500
We're almost there. It's just over there.

240
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,170
My dad says

241
00:19:24,170 --> 00:19:28,670
men who bother women are the pettiest and worst kind of human beings in the world.

242
00:19:28,670 --> 00:19:32,010
I'll pay the taxi fare. Let's take a taxi, yeah?

243
00:19:32,010 --> 00:19:33,930
But it's just right over there.

244
00:19:33,930 --> 00:19:36,840
You keep saying it's right here, right there.

245
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:38,640
Child, Hyo Seon!

246
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:40,360
Hyo Seon!

247
00:19:42,230 --> 00:19:45,820
What a ruckus! The president is fuming.

248
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:49,020
He has all the staff at home on their knees.

249
00:19:49,020 --> 00:19:52,560
He hasn't even allowed any food since lunch time.

250
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:55,200
From lunch until now?

251
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:57,060
What to do?

252
00:19:57,060 --> 00:20:01,060
Oh my, hey you. Where are you going?

253
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,960
She really...

254
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:08,900
- It's this way.
- Hurry.

255
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,940
I can't sell this kind of alcohol.

256
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:14,900
How can you call this wine?

257
00:20:17,380 --> 00:20:19,960
Boss, please don't do this.

258
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,900
This kid.

259
00:20:23,830 --> 00:20:29,640
If you put in rice, yeast and water and mix them up, does that just make rice wine?

260
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:33,070
Is anything with two eyes and a nose a human being?

261
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:38,430
Whether it is angry or crestfallen, you must check the temperature and humidity frequently

262
00:20:38,430 --> 00:20:40,170
and you must tend to it and nurse it, I told you.

263
00:20:40,170 --> 00:20:45,450
Why did you mindessly neglect it and create this craziness?

264
00:20:45,450 --> 00:20:49,760
This isn't alcohol! This is sewage!

265
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:02,760
Dad!

266
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,230
Dad, Dad.

267
00:21:05,230 --> 00:21:07,730
Who brought her in here?!

268
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:10,290
Dad, stop it.

269
00:21:10,290 --> 00:21:14,590
I asked who brought her here? Did you, Grannies?

270
00:21:15,950 --> 00:21:20,350
Dad, Ahjussis... their knees must be hurting.

271
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:22,690
You go home.

272
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,290
Dad.

273
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:41,730
Among those kneeling men,

274
00:21:42,770 --> 00:21:47,090
half of them are my friends' dads.

275
00:22:09,850 --> 00:22:11,670
Dad.

276
00:22:12,930 --> 00:22:16,390
I don't want to even see your faces. All of you get lost.

277
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,790
Dad...

278
00:22:19,790 --> 00:22:22,930
Dad.

279
00:22:22,930 --> 00:22:24,860
Dad.

280
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:29,110
Dad.

281
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:35,150
Mr, are you okay?

282
00:22:35,150 --> 00:22:36,680
Are you okay?

283
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:38,040
Ahjussi...

284
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:43,460
Our president, when his wife was alive, he was not that nasty.

285
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:48,470
All of you must be hungry. Hurry to the dining room.

286
00:22:48,470 --> 00:22:53,170
Grandma, did the mother here pass away?

287
00:22:54,390 --> 00:22:58,870
When Hyo Seon was 8 years old.

288
00:23:00,990 --> 00:23:04,270
But, who are you?

289
00:23:04,270 --> 00:23:06,350
I am sorry.

290
00:23:09,330 --> 00:23:14,130
Ajumma, I forgot.

291
00:23:14,130 --> 00:23:17,920
No, it's fine. I see that this was an important matter.

292
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:20,960
Yes. Quickly, come to my house with me.

293
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:23,040
Okay. Is your house far?

294
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:25,970
It can be far, let's go slowly.

295
00:23:25,970 --> 00:23:29,000
Far? It really is just over there.

296
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,600
Over there.

297
00:23:35,150 --> 00:23:37,400
Is that place really...

298
00:23:38,470 --> 00:23:40,380
It was really close then.

299
00:23:40,380 --> 00:23:41,870
Yes.

300
00:23:47,370 --> 00:23:49,220
Come along.

301
00:23:52,530 --> 00:23:54,290
Just a moment.

302
00:23:54,290 --> 00:23:56,680
I'll be right back.

303
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:49,700
Where did it go? Where did it go? Where did it go?

304
00:25:03,130 --> 00:25:04,380
Yes, like that.

305
00:25:04,380 --> 00:25:05,440
That's right.

306
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:07,420
You seem to have a lot of work.

307
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:10,350
Should I help you a little bit?

308
00:25:10,350 --> 00:25:14,340
But who are you?

309
00:25:23,920 --> 00:25:27,430
I... never lost it.

310
00:25:27,430 --> 00:25:31,540
There's nothing that I've lost forever.

311
00:25:42,120 --> 00:25:45,430
Because I'm opening mom's stuff for the first time in a long time,

312
00:25:45,430 --> 00:25:48,510
I don't think it will be in here.

313
00:26:08,980 --> 00:26:12,060
Bible

314
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:30,060
The bag I took to the class trip!

315
00:26:31,270 --> 00:26:33,120
Where was it?

316
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:39,880
Where did it go?

317
00:26:50,220 --> 00:26:51,470
Aigoo, what to do?

318
00:26:51,470 --> 00:26:55,170
- Aigoo, what to do?
- Missus, you sure are strange.

319
00:26:55,170 --> 00:26:58,400
Why get in the way of the water being thrown away?

320
00:26:58,400 --> 00:27:00,820
I'm really sorry.

321
00:27:00,820 --> 00:27:03,810
I was trying to help you...

322
00:27:04,550 --> 00:27:08,040
It's okay. I can just dry it off.

323
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:11,430
It does smell a bit fishy but,

324
00:27:13,220 --> 00:27:15,860
the fish smell is very potent.

325
00:27:17,570 --> 00:27:19,930
What's wrong, Ajumma?

326
00:27:33,230 --> 00:27:39,220
You said these are your late mother's clothes, so I don't know if it's okay for me to be wearing these.

327
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:50,630
I'll only wear these until my clothes are dry.

328
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:56,170
What's wrong?

329
00:27:58,350 --> 00:28:03,150
You're... really pretty.

330
00:28:03,150 --> 00:28:05,680
Right, thank you.

331
00:28:07,250 --> 00:28:10,910
Ahjumma, you resemble Hwang Shin Hye (doll-like type).

332
00:28:10,910 --> 00:28:15,490
Omo, kid, how can that be? I resemble Jeong Yoon Hee (voluptuous type).

333
00:28:16,550 --> 00:28:21,140
My mom looked like Hwang Shin Hye too.

334
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:28,510
Right, I often hear that I look like Hwang Shin Hye, too.

335
00:28:35,100 --> 00:28:37,650
Omo, child,

336
00:28:37,650 --> 00:28:40,230
What's wrong?

337
00:28:40,230 --> 00:28:42,350
What is?

338
00:28:42,350 --> 00:28:45,760
Did I do something wrong?

339
00:28:51,310 --> 00:28:56,990
The clothes really suit you well.

340
00:28:58,450 --> 00:29:01,350
Right, thank you.

341
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:07,000
The clothes really do suit you well.

342
00:29:08,230 --> 00:29:11,290
Why are you crying so much?

343
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:17,410
I don't know.

344
00:29:19,250 --> 00:29:23,280
My tears just keep coming out.

345
00:29:29,130 --> 00:29:32,350
Don't cry, hm? Don't cry.

346
00:29:32,350 --> 00:29:34,430
Don't cry.

347
00:29:34,430 --> 00:29:36,460
Don't cry...

348
00:29:50,190 --> 00:29:52,740
Please do it again.

349
00:29:54,330 --> 00:29:55,960
Hm?

350
00:30:00,210 --> 00:30:02,410
Please do this for me.

351
00:30:33,710 --> 00:30:35,830
Please wait here for a moment.

352
00:30:35,830 --> 00:30:38,730
Okay, thank you.

353
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:02,860
Go in, Ajumma.

354
00:31:02,860 --> 00:31:05,620
Okay, thank you.

355
00:31:15,170 --> 00:31:16,910
Who is she?

356
00:31:23,990 --> 00:31:28,030
Uncle, have you not seen my travel bag?

357
00:31:28,030 --> 00:31:29,030
Huh?

358
00:31:29,030 --> 00:31:31,380
My travel bag.

359
00:31:31,380 --> 00:31:37,690
What Oppa Gi Hoon bought me, the one with green plaids, haven't you seen it?

360
00:31:37,690 --> 00:31:40,950
Oh, that one! You took it to the attic the last time.

361
00:31:40,950 --> 00:31:42,830
Shall I find it for you?

362
00:31:44,210 --> 00:31:47,550
No, lock it up.

363
00:31:47,550 --> 00:31:49,010
Pardon?

364
00:31:49,010 --> 00:31:53,720
Lock it up. Hide it thoroughly, Uncle.

365
00:31:59,130 --> 00:32:03,160
What? What are you saying right now?

366
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:07,800
Are you saying the wine release might be put off to fall?

367
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:13,230
Look here, look here, it has to be marketed by summer no matter what.

368
00:32:13,230 --> 00:32:15,660
Do you know how much your monthly pay is?

369
00:32:15,660 --> 00:32:19,900
Do you want me to show what happens if you try to take other people's money for nothing?

370
00:32:19,900 --> 00:32:21,930
This won't do.

371
00:32:21,930 --> 00:32:25,180
Forget about going home and wait right there. I will be at the lab straight away.

372
00:32:25,180 --> 00:32:26,810
Hang up.

373
00:32:48,700 --> 00:32:50,490
I'm sorry.

374
00:32:50,490 --> 00:32:54,520
I was waiting until you finished your phone call.

375
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:58,780
Who...?

376
00:32:58,780 --> 00:33:01,030
Hyo Seon...

377
00:33:02,250 --> 00:33:06,040
Hyo Seon?

378
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:09,390
But, what's the problem..?

379
00:33:09,390 --> 00:33:11,360
For a person she didn't know,

380
00:33:11,360 --> 00:33:15,220
because she agreed to keep a thing without knowing anything about it,

381
00:33:15,220 --> 00:33:18,350
I heard that you scolded her very much.

382
00:33:19,300 --> 00:33:22,350
That... Hyo Seon

383
00:33:22,350 --> 00:33:25,570
said from some girl of the same age as Hyo Seon...

384
00:33:25,570 --> 00:33:29,700
Yes, I am that child's mother.

385
00:33:33,380 --> 00:33:37,480
We had a situation, but its not a bad object.

386
00:33:37,480 --> 00:33:39,730
If you don't believe me, there's nothing I can do about it.

387
00:33:39,730 --> 00:33:43,570
Anyway, I'm sorry.

388
00:34:06,120 --> 00:34:14,190
Also, I know these words might be a bit surprising on our first meeting but

389
00:34:14,190 --> 00:34:16,760
I have a favour to ask you.

390
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:21,060
Of course, there's nothing I can do if you reject me

391
00:34:25,070 --> 00:34:32,800
I heard that the bag with the item I left to your daughter was loaned to a friend who lives far away.

392
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:36,420
It will take some time before she finds it.

393
00:34:36,420 --> 00:34:41,570
I have nowhere else to run.

394
00:34:41,570 --> 00:34:46,200
While I'm waiting, could I not work here?

395
00:34:46,200 --> 00:34:50,640
Kitchen work or any other work will be fine.

396
00:34:54,710 --> 00:35:01,520
I know how ridiculous my words may seem...

397
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:24,360
I told you no.

398
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:26,990
I am here.

399
00:35:27,870 --> 00:35:32,060
I am here, so there's no reason my mom wouldn't come.

400
00:35:32,060 --> 00:35:35,300
She says the business is just taking longer.

401
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:41,630
Do you trust your mom?

402
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:44,080
What did you say?

403
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:49,920
Because you are here, do you think your mom

404
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:56,790
will return here no matter what because of you...

405
00:35:56,790 --> 00:35:59,010
Do you believe that?

406
00:35:59,850 --> 00:36:02,030
Of course.

407
00:36:06,390 --> 00:36:08,960
Your mom,

408
00:36:12,660 --> 00:36:15,620
has she never abandoned you?

409
00:36:17,330 --> 00:36:19,450
She hasn't.

410
00:36:19,450 --> 00:36:22,110
She would never.

411
00:36:23,270 --> 00:36:28,090
Then, that's fine.

412
00:36:34,910 --> 00:36:37,020
What are you doing right now?!

413
00:36:37,020 --> 00:36:39,420
Are you not leaving?

414
00:36:40,330 --> 00:36:42,370
Jeong Woo!

415
00:36:42,370 --> 00:36:44,610
Jeong Woo!!!

416
00:36:52,460 --> 00:36:55,780
I can't do this, lose some fat!

417
00:37:09,870 --> 00:37:13,710
Your call could not be connected...

418
00:37:13,710 --> 00:37:17,440
Once connected to the voice mailbox, you will be charged.

419
00:37:46,860 --> 00:37:49,420
Hyo Seon is home!

420
00:37:53,190 --> 00:37:56,930
Where is she?

421
00:37:59,030 --> 00:38:00,780
Oppa!

422
00:38:17,230 --> 00:38:19,030
You came?

423
00:38:28,170 --> 00:38:30,490
I'm hurt.

424
00:38:32,740 --> 00:38:35,090
I got hurt..

425
00:38:39,050 --> 00:38:40,810
All done.

426
00:38:41,850 --> 00:38:44,810
I want to see it.

427
00:38:47,410 --> 00:38:49,670
I am going to keep it.

428
00:40:52,780 --> 00:41:00,070
Daeseong True Wine Makers

429
00:41:26,870 --> 00:41:29,500
Seeing that your lights are on...

430
00:41:30,490 --> 00:41:32,260
What...

431
00:41:32,260 --> 00:41:38,080
Today is Hyo Sun's painting competition, so I promised to make her a lunch box.

432
00:41:38,080 --> 00:41:42,900
But I didn't have time to go grocery shopping. Can you give me the directions?

433
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:47,120
It's far.

434
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:51,440
It's okay. I can just walk there slowly.

435
00:42:13,620 --> 00:42:16,340
I can go by myself though...

436
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:57,440
Oh, I'm scared.

437
00:43:11,050 --> 00:43:12,580
Aigoo, what are you doing?

438
00:43:37,750 --> 00:43:39,380
What's wrong?

439
00:43:39,380 --> 00:43:41,560
Oppa.

440
00:43:48,220 --> 00:43:50,880
Uncle...

441
00:43:50,880 --> 00:43:54,760
gave Ajumma Song Kang Sook the ring.

442
00:43:58,870 --> 00:44:02,650
Thank you for everything. - Song Kang Sook.

443
00:44:32,670 --> 00:44:37,190
The last train is in thirty minutes and the last bus is in an hour.

444
00:44:37,190 --> 00:44:42,150
I can just go to the train station and you can go to the bus station.

445
00:44:42,150 --> 00:44:44,530
I don't want to hear it so get out.

446
00:44:44,530 --> 00:44:48,360
Hyo Seon can't handle the situation right now.

447
00:44:48,360 --> 00:44:52,320
She's always like that when a guest leaves.

448
00:44:52,320 --> 00:44:55,380
I'll escort her for now.

449
00:44:56,200 --> 00:44:58,190
What's with you, punk?

450
00:45:00,690 --> 00:45:06,260
Hyo Seon has been happy as if she has become a seven year old kid lately.

451
00:45:07,670 --> 00:45:12,520
She's a seven year old kid separated from her Mom..

452
00:45:12,520 --> 00:45:16,300
Be quiet and don't do anything.

453
00:45:16,300 --> 00:45:17,980
How can she leave without saying anything?

454
00:45:17,980 --> 00:45:22,630
How can a person do that? Why would you go look for a person who decided to do that?

455
00:45:22,630 --> 00:45:27,390
No matter what you do, I'm going to the train station.

456
00:45:39,480 --> 00:45:42,820
Tell me I'll see her again.

457
00:45:44,220 --> 00:45:47,920
It'll work out the way you say it will.

458
00:45:47,920 --> 00:45:50,820
Tell me she's coming. Quickly!

459
00:45:52,660 --> 00:45:57,290
Quickly tell me that she's coming.

460
00:46:07,750 --> 00:46:09,120
What was it...

461
00:46:09,120 --> 00:46:13,540
Even though you knew the kid was kidding around and hid it, why are you pretending not to know?

462
00:46:13,540 --> 00:46:15,510
What was the purpose?

463
00:46:15,510 --> 00:46:20,460
Since you've been here because of this the whole time, now that you have it back, you can take it and leave then.

464
00:46:25,690 --> 00:46:31,690
I want to go my way, but I can't do that, Goo Dae Seong.

465
00:46:53,350 --> 00:46:55,270
You're leaving?

466
00:46:58,340 --> 00:47:00,410
How can you leave like this?

467
00:47:00,410 --> 00:47:03,440
You got attached to the kid. How can you...?

468
00:47:03,440 --> 00:47:06,030
I've imposed on you a lot.

469
00:47:06,030 --> 00:47:09,420
I have left Hyo Seon's mom's clothes all mended.

470
00:47:09,420 --> 00:47:11,540
The kid's crying.

471
00:47:11,540 --> 00:47:15,140
My daughter is probably crying right now too.

472
00:47:15,140 --> 00:47:18,200
You can just bring your child here then.

473
00:47:19,040 --> 00:47:23,170
The man I lived with is holding onto my child.

474
00:47:23,170 --> 00:47:25,320
It won't be easy to bring her here.

475
00:47:25,320 --> 00:47:28,470
I told you I'll bring her here. I will.

476
00:47:30,780 --> 00:47:36,240
Is this solely because of Hyo Seon?

477
00:47:38,620 --> 00:47:43,890
Are you only telling me to stay here because of Hyo Seon?

478
00:48:47,200 --> 00:48:50,880
Give me rice! I only ate kimchi so I'm hungry.

479
00:48:50,880 --> 00:48:52,700
Move it.

480
00:48:56,620 --> 00:48:59,790
Still, you don't have a single thing to worry about.

481
00:48:59,790 --> 00:49:02,220
I'll take responsibility for you.

482
00:49:02,220 --> 00:49:03,150
Get lost.

483
00:49:03,150 --> 00:49:06,930
Don't they say, though, a widower best knows a widow's circumstances?

484
00:49:08,250 --> 00:49:13,460
What? My mom left me with that Hairball and ran away.

485
00:49:13,460 --> 00:49:16,430
Your mom, too, done left you with that Hairball

486
00:49:16,430 --> 00:49:19,150
and done ran away, no?

487
00:49:19,150 --> 00:49:23,090
So my mom ran away?

488
00:49:23,090 --> 00:49:25,170
Yes.

489
00:49:25,170 --> 00:49:28,390
Abandoning me?
Yes!

490
00:49:32,160 --> 00:49:34,040
Are you sure?

491
00:49:34,040 --> 00:49:37,330
Why do you keep making me say the same thing?

492
00:49:53,210 --> 00:49:55,360
Long live.

493
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:27,770
Your mom isn't even here. Where are you going?

494
00:50:27,770 --> 00:50:28,780
To run away.

495
00:50:28,780 --> 00:50:30,440
By yourself?

496
00:50:30,440 --> 00:50:32,100
Because I'm by myself.

497
00:50:32,100 --> 00:50:34,970
Because I'm alone, I'm running away.

498
00:50:34,970 --> 00:50:39,000
If I don't have my mom, I can be happy.

499
00:50:42,790 --> 00:50:44,730
That's not right.

500
00:50:44,730 --> 00:50:46,990
What are you doing?

501
00:50:46,990 --> 00:50:49,790
I can't send you alone.

502
00:50:49,790 --> 00:50:50,690
What?

503
00:50:50,690 --> 00:50:55,330
Didn't I say I can't send you off alone? Quickly unpack your things.

504
00:50:58,860 --> 00:51:00,950
Are you not going to let go?

505
00:51:06,070 --> 00:51:10,900
I'll let go...

506
00:51:16,460 --> 00:51:20,920
Look here. I've done all that I can.

507
00:51:20,920 --> 00:51:26,380
I made a lot of food, and I prepared enough kimchi for the two of you to eat for a few months.

508
00:51:26,380 --> 00:51:29,560
I did all the laundry and cleaning.

509
00:51:29,560 --> 00:51:36,150
I also filled up the fridge with a lot of alcohol so you can drown in alcohol for three months.

510
00:51:36,150 --> 00:51:37,820
That's all then, right?

511
00:51:38,640 --> 00:51:41,050
I don't have any debt to you.

512
00:51:44,790 --> 00:51:48,780
If you think of the ring as debt...

513
00:51:48,780 --> 00:51:51,600
then find my Mom and get it from her.

514
00:51:52,510 --> 00:51:54,780
Not me.

515
00:52:00,860 --> 00:52:04,740
Nui, nui!

516
00:52:04,740 --> 00:52:06,920
Nui!

517
00:52:08,470 --> 00:52:11,500
If you follow me, you're dead.

518
00:52:11,500 --> 00:52:13,850
Nui ...

519
00:52:21,220 --> 00:52:23,720
Song Eun Joo, student?

520
00:52:51,920 --> 00:52:57,250
While living, there's stuff one must and must not do.

521
00:52:57,250 --> 00:52:58,870
I try to be patient.

522
00:52:58,870 --> 00:53:03,920
Who does he think I am?

523
00:53:03,920 --> 00:53:08,740
But what's the reason for asking me especially to do this?

524
00:53:12,750 --> 00:53:17,520
Lean your back on the back rest and go comfortably. You look uncomfortable.

525
00:53:17,520 --> 00:53:23,000
Leave your bag next to you. If you're sleepy, you can sleep comfortably.

526
00:53:25,280 --> 00:53:27,560
I want to go to the restroom

527
00:53:27,560 --> 00:53:29,290
Huh?

528
00:53:29,290 --> 00:53:31,240
Restroom.

529
00:53:35,740 --> 00:53:37,170
Ah, look at this.

530
00:53:37,170 --> 00:53:41,960
Women's restroom

531
00:53:46,200 --> 00:53:50,990
Wow, really. Isn't she pulling out everything from her stomach?

532
00:53:50,990 --> 00:53:53,320
How long ago did she go in?

533
00:53:55,060 --> 00:53:56,860
I won't stop.

534
00:53:56,860 --> 00:54:00,790
Even if I have to spend the future searching for food in trash cans

535
00:54:00,790 --> 00:54:02,520
I will never go to my mom Song Kang Sook

536
00:54:02,520 --> 00:54:06,470
in the house of whatever good-for-nothing man

537
00:54:06,470 --> 00:54:08,630
whom that woman grabbed the ankle of,

538
00:54:08,630 --> 00:54:10,560
Just a moment!

539
00:54:11,760 --> 00:54:14,460
Wait a minute and stop for a moment!

540
00:55:21,140 --> 00:55:23,800
Ah! Let go!

541
00:55:36,150 --> 00:55:39,910
Your mother won't just follow you easily.

542
00:55:39,910 --> 00:55:45,800
She warned me and asked me to take you carefully, saying you might run away. I guess she was right.

543
00:55:48,200 --> 00:55:52,000
Do you have somewhere to go? Do you have money?

544
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:58,110
Are you thinking when you go somewhere on your last day, there's nothing I won't do to survive?

545
00:56:02,520 --> 00:56:06,390
That's... not easy.

546
00:56:07,520 --> 00:56:12,570
Even if you go somewhere, they won't accept you as a minor.

547
00:56:13,650 --> 00:56:18,500
Even if you work to death you don't know whether you will make a lot of money or not.

548
00:56:19,540 --> 00:56:22,210
The expenses are not cheap.

549
00:56:24,410 --> 00:56:30,390
It'll change a bit as soon as you turn 20, so just endure it for a little bit.

550
00:56:30,390 --> 00:56:33,580
How about leaving home once you turn 20?

551
00:56:36,880 --> 00:56:38,430
Huh?

552
00:56:40,860 --> 00:56:45,340
It's weird. It's really weird,

553
00:56:46,410 --> 00:56:50,020
Even if he says the moon is rectangular, I want to believe him.

554
00:56:51,320 --> 00:56:56,170
I must be possessed by a ghost.

555
00:56:56,170 --> 00:56:59,760
I should've just jumped out of the train then and there!

556
00:57:01,220 --> 00:57:03,040
Be quiet.

557
00:57:03,040 --> 00:57:05,280
This time, how far will we go?

558
00:57:05,280 --> 00:57:08,370
If we get thrown out of here again or runaway, it's one or the other.

559
00:57:08,370 --> 00:57:11,980
How fare are we going to go this time? 3 months? 4 months?

560
00:57:11,980 --> 00:57:13,890
I told you this person is not like that!

561
00:57:13,890 --> 00:57:16,310
It's not like that?! What's not like that?!

562
00:57:16,310 --> 00:57:20,160
Looking from the back, what's the difference between this man and any other man?

563
00:57:20,160 --> 00:57:22,300
Mom, just please!

564
00:57:22,300 --> 00:57:25,410
Let's not get attached to men who aren't human just to eat a meal, huh?

565
00:57:25,410 --> 00:57:28,810
Just you and I can somehow survive.

566
00:57:28,810 --> 00:57:29,860
Are you not going to lower your voice?!

567
00:57:29,860 --> 00:57:32,700
I don't want to! I won't do it. Mom, you can just do it alone.

568
00:57:32,700 --> 00:57:34,960
Who am I doing this for!

569
00:57:34,960 --> 00:57:37,980
Lies! The lies that you do it for me,

570
00:57:37,980 --> 00:57:41,220
I need to sew your lips together in order not to hear you!

571
00:57:41,220 --> 00:57:44,140
What?

572
00:57:44,140 --> 00:57:44,940
Let go!

573
00:57:44,940 --> 00:57:47,430
Come here! Follow me!

574
00:57:47,430 --> 00:57:49,130
- Come.
- Let me go!

575
00:57:49,130 --> 00:57:51,280
-Let me go!
-Come here.

576
00:57:51,280 --> 00:57:52,960
Let go!

577
00:57:52,960 --> 00:57:55,900
-This wench, this wench!
-Don't do this.

578
00:57:55,900 --> 00:57:59,720
You don't realize all the effort I have put in to survive.

579
00:57:59,720 --> 00:58:02,410
You're my daughter and what did you say? You'll sew my lips together?

580
00:58:02,410 --> 00:58:04,190
Who did I do all of this for?

581
00:58:04,190 --> 00:58:07,480
Don't say it's for me! Mom, do you live for me?!

582
00:58:07,480 --> 00:58:09,930
A mom that lived for me...

583
00:58:09,930 --> 00:58:11,470
Is that why you abandoned me?

584
00:58:11,470 --> 00:58:13,630
What? Abandon?

585
00:58:13,630 --> 00:58:15,760
When did I abandon you?

586
00:58:15,760 --> 00:58:19,270
Since I gave birth to you without your father, I've never once thought of abandoning you!

587
00:58:19,270 --> 00:58:21,690
Even If I knew because of you my future was doomed,

588
00:58:21,690 --> 00:58:23,080
I've never once thought of abandoning you!

589
00:58:23,080 --> 00:58:25,110
You left me alone at that house!

590
00:58:25,110 --> 00:58:27,230
With that creepy hairball!

591
00:58:27,230 --> 00:58:29,780
I was taken as a hostage.

592
00:58:29,780 --> 00:58:33,420
Do you know how disgusting I felt?

593
00:58:38,620 --> 00:58:41,950
That human... perhaps did he

594
00:58:44,060 --> 00:58:45,500
do something weird to you?

595
00:58:45,500 --> 00:58:48,890
How scared was I that he might!

596
00:58:50,520 --> 00:58:53,540
Okay. No matter how rough Mr. Kang may have been,

597
00:58:53,540 --> 00:58:56,360
he wasn't as bad as son of a bitch when we lived in Daejon.

598
00:58:56,360 --> 00:58:59,350
I know that. Since I knew that I left you there alone.

599
00:58:59,350 --> 00:59:02,940
Lies. It doesn't matter, what happens to me.

600
00:59:02,940 --> 00:59:07,390
Whether I starve or eat, sleep or wake up

601
00:59:07,390 --> 00:59:10,310
Why did you call me? Why did you call?!

602
00:59:10,310 --> 00:59:14,190
I'm going to go. You can live and eat well yourself.

603
00:59:14,190 --> 00:59:17,440
Did you hear the last words I said to your dad?

604
00:59:20,870 --> 00:59:24,960
Now, we don't have to go to beggar-like men for food.

605
00:59:24,960 --> 00:59:28,830
We don't have to sleep in motels escaping from them.

606
00:59:28,830 --> 00:59:33,420
You can attend school properly too.

607
00:59:33,420 --> 00:59:37,130
This is the last one. There's nowhere else.

608
00:59:39,500 --> 00:59:41,990
There's really no other place?

609
00:59:41,990 --> 00:59:43,850
There isn't.

610
00:59:47,940 --> 00:59:54,410
If we're kicked out of here or run away again, then let me go.

611
00:59:54,410 --> 00:59:58,020
Do you think you'd be able to live without me, you wench?

612
00:59:58,020 --> 01:00:00,320
Let me go. Say that you'll let me go.

613
01:00:00,320 --> 01:00:03,550
Then, I'll be your daughter for now.

614
01:00:03,550 --> 01:00:07,250
Fine, I'll let you go. I'll do that for you.

615
01:00:09,690 --> 01:00:12,890
This time, how beggar-like is that man?

616
01:00:38,320 --> 01:00:43,690
Whatever is it, please say something nice.

617
01:00:50,300 --> 01:00:52,530
You're the elder.

618
01:00:57,870 --> 01:01:01,410
I, with your mother,

619
01:01:04,330 --> 01:01:10,780
had one daughter but it's become two.

620
01:01:14,270 --> 01:01:16,650
I'm not sure ...

621
01:01:19,970 --> 01:01:25,070
What would you like me to do first?

622
01:01:25,070 --> 01:01:28,300
Whatever it is,

623
01:01:28,300 --> 01:01:30,790
I want to try and do it well for you.

624
01:01:31,730 --> 01:01:36,860
If you tell me what you want, I promise I will try within my greatest efforts-

625
01:01:36,860 --> 01:01:39,560
I don't need anything like a promise.

626
01:01:43,900 --> 01:01:46,790
I don't trust things like that.

627
01:01:46,790 --> 01:01:52,330
Don't think of doing anything like a promise, but just let me attend school.

628
01:01:57,960 --> 01:02:03,110
He felt very sad hearing me say that you have not been attending school regularly.

629
01:02:03,110 --> 01:02:07,690
We prepared everything so that you would be able to attend first thing tomorrow.

630
01:02:15,570 --> 01:02:18,100
Hyo Seon is back!

631
01:02:41,650 --> 01:02:44,530
Unni, hi!

632
01:02:57,380 --> 01:03:04,720
♫ It must be you. I can't be without you. ♫

633
01:03:04,720 --> 01:03:10,940
♫ Like this for another day, month or year ♫

634
01:03:11,760 --> 01:03:13,910
♫ I don't mind even if I am hurt. ♫

635
01:03:13,910 --> 01:03:15,750
It's amazing.

636
01:03:15,750 --> 01:03:17,190
Sis, where are you going?
♫  don't mind even if my heart breaks ♫

637
01:03:17,190 --> 01:03:18,400
Don't be like that.

638
01:03:18,400 --> 01:03:21,920
Since I'm already being called trash, I might as well live as trash.

639
01:03:21,920 --> 01:03:25,450
Unni!

640
01:03:25,450 --> 01:03:31,390
Until everything is arranged, don't get the marriage license.

641
01:03:31,390 --> 01:03:37,620
Since I don't know when I'll be kicked out or need to run away, I'm telling you to do it when there's a chance.

642
01:03:37,620 --> 01:03:39,700
Who am I?

643
01:03:39,700 --> 01:03:44,200
When I talk to her, she's a bit weird.

644
01:03:44,200 --> 01:03:47,290
Our Eun Jo... besides her mother,

645
01:03:47,290 --> 01:03:50,030
she has no one else to call.

646
01:03:51,150 --> 01:03:56,190
♫ Even if I live again ♫
